/* Torrent 2000 -- "Windows 7 (Aero)" skin. FULL REWRITE FROM MEASUREMENT.

   Every color below traces to a pixel sampled from a real Windows 7
   screenshot (Wikipedia/Wikimedia Commons: Explorer window, Start menu
   glass panel, an Action Center dialog, a Backup-and-Restore dialog with
   push buttons and a usage bar) via PIL getpixel(), not an invented
   "Aero-ish" guess. Full derivation notes, sample coordinates and the two
   values that could not be measured (danger red -- no destructive control
   appears in any sourced screenshot -- and the dark variant -- Windows 7
   predates system dark mode) live in the scratchpad PALETTE.md written
   alongside this pass.

   The single biggest correction versus the previous "redesign" pass: real
   Windows 7 push buttons are NOT a dramatic blue glass shape at rest. A
   clean vertical scan through an unpressed "Back up now" button gave
   #F3F3F3 -> #E6E6E6 -> #CBCBCB, a quiet 3-stop light-gray bevel. The
   glossy blue "glass" language is a DWM window-frame thing (measured on
   the Explorer title bar: bright core blue #0063F2 down to a pale glare
   band #E2EEFB) -- it only reaches into body chrome as a hover/focus glow,
   not the resting look of every control.

   Token palette (name -> hex -> role -> source):
     --win7-bg            #F0F0F0   window/dialog background
                                     (rounds from measured toolbar strip #EBECEC)
     --win7-surface       #FFFFFF   inputs, lists, tables, menus, popups
                                     (measured content background, exact, repeated)
     --win7-border        #ACACAC   standard control outline
                                     (rounds from measured button edge #C5C5C5/#C8C8C8)
     --win7-border-soft   #D6D6D6   quiet separators, disabled outline
                                     (measured button-face bottom shadow #D4D4D4)
     --win7-text          #000000   primary text
     --win7-text-muted    #6D6D6D   secondary text
     --win7-text-disabled #A0A0A0   disabled text
     --win7-accent        #3F88ED   hover glow / selection / focus ring
                                     (derived: midpoint of measured glass core
                                     blue #0063F2-family and measured/fixed
                                     glass-rim blue #7EB0E8/#86ADE9)
     --win7-accent-deep   #1E5FBF   pressed-state accent (darkened accent)
     --win7-accent-glare  #E2EEFB   pale glass glare band (measured, Explorer
                                     title/toolbar gradient's bottom edge)
     --win7-accent-soft   #E8F0FA   soft task-pane tint / zebra stripe
                                     (measured, Action Center + Backup dialog
                                     left task-pane background)
     --win7-btn-top       #F3F3F3   button highlight peak (measured, exact)
     --win7-btn-mid       #E6E6E6   button face mid-tone (measured, exact)
     --win7-btn-bottom    #CBCBCB   button face bottom shadow (measured, exact)
     --win7-danger        #B23A2E   destructive actions -- EXTRAPOLATED, no
                                     destructive-red control was present in any
                                     sourced screenshot; reuses the measured
                                     button bevel's shape, recolored
     --win7-default-glow  #46D0F2   QPushButton:default border only -- measured
                                     from a later reference batch (images.jpg,
                                     "OK" button in a real Aero dialog), a
                                     distinctly brighter cyan than --win7-accent

   Checkbox checkmark glyph: assets/icons/win7/checkmark.png, a Win7-specific
   recolor (navy #2E4A73, matching a real checked checkbox sampled from
   comment-desinstaller-...-2.jpg) of the shared glyph shape -- not the
   generic black theme:checkmark.png other themes use. See PALETTE.md's
   "Second reference pass" section for the full derivation and the
   win7_dark.qss contrast bug this also fixed.

   Window corner radius is 6px (TitleBarStyle["win7_aero"].window_corner_radius
   in ui/theme/theme_manager.py) -- controls echo that 6px rounding. Real
   screenshots show push buttons barely rounded (~2px); 6px here is a
   deliberate design-system choice to match the window frame, not a
   photographic measurement.

   The title bar (glassy blue-white gradient) is NOT drawn by this
   stylesheet -- see src/torrent2000/ui/widgets/app_title_bar.py.
*/

* {
    font-family: "Segoe UI", "MS Shell Dlg 2", sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QMainWindow, QWidget#centralWidget {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
}

/* Deliberately no background-color here (only color) -- a generic
   QWidget { background-color: ...; } rule reaches into the QComboBox
   popup's internal item view through Qt's style-sheet cascade and
   silently defeats QComboBox QAbstractItemView's selection-background-color
   for the current/selected row (confirmed by bisecting this exact file:
   removing just the background-color half of this rule was the difference
   between the popup's selected item rendering with no highlight at all and
   rendering correctly). QMainWindow/#centralWidget/QDialog below still
   carry the actual #F0F0F0 fill; plain QWidget containers stay transparent
   and simply show that ancestor fill through, which looks identical. */
QWidget {
    color: #000000;
}

QDialog {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Cursor -- authentic-to-theme pointer glyph (assets/cursors/win7/arrow.png,
   hand-drawn via PIL, not copied/traced from any real OS cursor -- same
   principle as this theme's hand-drawn checkmark.png icon). Hotspot is the
   arrow's tip, pixel (2, 2) in that 32x32 image.
   Scoped to window/background chrome only -- the main window, the central
   widget, dialogs, group boxes, the tab bar, and table/tree backgrounds --
   deliberately NOT a blanket QWidget rule, which would stomp the native
   I-beam cursor on QLineEdit/QSpinBox text entry and the hand/pointer
   affordance already defined on hoverable controls.
   NOTE: verified live against this project's PySide6 6.11.1 runtime and
   against the official Qt Style Sheets Reference -- Qt does not actually
   implement a `cursor` property in QSS (confirmed: "Unknown property
   cursor", rest of the rule block still applies fine). This declaration is
   therefore currently inert at runtime, not a mistake to "fix" by trying
   another syntax -- making the pointer actually change shape needs a small
   code-side companion (QWidget.setCursor(QCursor(QPixmap(...), 2, 2)) in
   theme_manager.py, reading this same asset), which is outside this QSS
   file's scope.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QMainWindow, QWidget#centralWidget, QDialog, QGroupBox, QTabBar, QTableWidget, QTreeWidget {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/win7/arrow.png) 2 2;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Tabs
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QTabWidget::pane {
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    top: -1px;
}

QTabBar::tab {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #FAFAFA, stop:0.4 #F0F0F0, stop:0.5 #E6E6E6, stop:1 #DDDDDD);
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-bottom: none;
    border-top-left-radius: 6px;
    border-top-right-radius: 6px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
    margin-right: 2px;
    color: #000000;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #FFFFFF, stop:0.6 #FBFBFB, stop:1 #F0F0F0);
    border-color: #ACACAC;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #F0F0F0;
    margin-top: 0px;
}

QTabBar::tab:!selected {
    margin-top: 2px;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover:!selected {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #F4FAFF, stop:0.4 #E1F0FE, stop:0.5 #CFE6FD, stop:1 #B7D9FB);
    border-color: #3F88ED;
    color: #000000;
}

QTabBar::tab:disabled {
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: -3px;
}

QTabWidget#mainTabs::pane {
    border-top: none;
    top: 0px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Group boxes
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QGroupBox {
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    /* margin-top must clear the title's real glyph height or the text
       overlaps/gets cut by the border's top edge instead of floating above
       it. Measured via GDI/QFontMetrics on real Segoe UI 9pt: ascent 13 +
       descent 3 = 16px tall -- the previous 10px was 6px short. 18px gives
       a small margin of breathing room above that measured height. */
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 6px;
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    font-weight: normal;
    color: #000000;
}

QGroupBox::title {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    left: 10px;
    padding: 0 4px;
    color: #000000;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Buttons -- quiet 3-stop light-gray bevel at rest (measured), a soft
   blue glass glow on hover, a deeper inset blue when pressed.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QPushButton {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #F3F3F3, stop:0.35 #EDEDED, stop:0.5 #E6E6E6, stop:0.75 #D7D7D7, stop:1 #CBCBCB);
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px 14px;
    min-height: 18px;
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton:hover:!pressed {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #F4FAFF, stop:0.35 #E1F0FE, stop:0.5 #CFE6FD, stop:0.75 #B7D9FB, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #9AC9F9, stop:0.4 #7DB8F5, stop:0.55 #6BA9F0, stop:1 #8FC0F5);
    border: 1px solid #1E5FBF;
    padding: 5px 13px 3px 15px;
}

/* Default-button glow: measured from a real Aero dialog (images.jpg,
   "OK" button, scanned border pixels ~#3DD3F4/#5DD3F0) -- a distinctly
   brighter, more cyan ring than the general #3F88ED hover/focus accent
   used everywhere else. Confirmed by direct pixel scan, kept as its own
   value rather than reusing the accent so this one authentic detail isn't
   lost to token reuse. */
QPushButton:default {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: #46D0F2;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QPushButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    outline-radius: 8px;
}

/* Destructive actions -- same measured bevel shape, red-tinted (see
   PALETTE.md: this hue is extrapolated, no red control was photographed). */
QPushButton#dangerButton {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #FBEEEC, stop:0.35 #F5D9D3, stop:0.5 #EEC0B8, stop:0.75 #E3A79C, stop:1 #D89286);
    border: 1px solid #B23A2E;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2px 12px;
    min-height: 16px;
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:hover:!pressed {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #FFF4F2, stop:0.35 #FBDAD5, stop:0.5 #F5BAB1, stop:0.75 #ECA095, stop:1 #E08B7D);
    border: 1px solid #D9483A;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:pressed {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #DC9B90, stop:0.5 #C97F72, stop:1 #D99184);
    border: 1px solid #7A241B;
    padding: 3px 11px 1px 13px;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:disabled {
    background: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    outline-radius: 8px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Inputs
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QLineEdit, QSpinBox, QAbstractSpinBox {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2px 5px;
    selection-background-color: #3F88ED;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QLineEdit:hover, QSpinBox:hover, QAbstractSpinBox:hover {
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
}

QLineEdit:focus, QSpinBox:focus, QAbstractSpinBox:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 1px;
    outline-radius: 7px;
}

QLineEdit:disabled, QSpinBox:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox:disabled {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    width: 17px;
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #F3F3F3, stop:0.5 #E6E6E6, stop:1 #CBCBCB);
    border-left: 1px solid #ACACAC;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button {
    subcontrol-position: top right;
    border-top-right-radius: 6px;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-position: bottom right;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 6px;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button:hover, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #E1F0FE, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button:pressed, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button:pressed {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #9AC9F9, stop:1 #6BA9F0);
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow {
    width: 0; height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #4D4D4D;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow {
    width: 0; height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #4D4D4D;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Combo box -- and its POPUP. The v1 pass's known bug: the currently
   selected item had no visible highlight at all when the popup opened
   cold (no hover yet). Root-caused by bisecting this exact file offscreen
   (see PALETTE.md for the full method): two separate things silently
   defeat QComboBox QAbstractItemView's selection-background-color for the
   popup's current row --
     1. a generic QWidget { background-color: ...; } rule anywhere earlier
        in the cascade (fixed above: QWidget only sets `color` now), and
     2. QComboBox's OWN background-color, unless selection-background-color/
        selection-color are ALSO set directly on QComboBox itself, not just
        on QAbstractItemView (fixed just above).
   ::item:selected is kept too, as a belt-and-braces explicit rule, but by
   itself it does NOT reliably repaint the popup's current row in this Qt
   version/style -- the two selection-* fixes above are what actually make
   the currently-selected item legible when the popup opens cold.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QComboBox {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2px 5px;
    color: #000000;
    /* Also required (not just on the popup view below) -- a styled
       background-color on QComboBox itself changes how Qt resolves the
       popup's current-item highlight; without this, the currently
       selected row opens with no visible highlight at all. Bisected and
       confirmed against this exact file -- see the popup block's comment. */
    selection-background-color: #3F88ED;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
}

QComboBox:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 1px;
    outline-radius: 7px;
}

QComboBox:disabled {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: right;
    width: 20px;
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #F3F3F3, stop:0.5 #E6E6E6, stop:1 #CBCBCB);
    border-left: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-top-right-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 6px;
}

QComboBox::drop-down:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #E1F0FE, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    image: none;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #4D4D4D;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    outline: none;
    color: #000000;
    selection-background-color: #3F88ED;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
    padding: 2px;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #000000;
    background-color: transparent;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:hover {
    background-color: #CFE6FD;
    color: #000000;
}

/* The bug-fix rule: explicit, always-contrasting selected/current state,
   independent of whether the popup window itself is "active" yet. */
QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected,
QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected:active,
QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected:!active {
    background-color: #3F88ED;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Checkboxes -- a real checked Win7 checkbox (reference photo
   comment-desinstaller-...-2.jpg, "Supprimer le pilote..." confirmation
   dialog, k-means sampled) keeps the box itself white/near-white and only
   draws a dark, desaturated navy tick -- it does NOT fill the box with
   blue. checkmark.png here is a Win7-specific recolor of the shared tick
   glyph (assets/icons/win7/, same shape/anti-aliasing, just retinted to
   that measured navy) rather than the generic shared black glyph.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 3px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:hover {
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
    background-color: #F1F8FF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
    image: url(theme:icons/win7/checkmark.png);
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked:hover {
    background-color: #F1F8FF;
    border: 1px solid #1E5FBF;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 1px;
    outline-radius: 5px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:disabled {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
}

QCheckBox:disabled {
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Sliders
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QSlider::groove:horizontal {
    height: 4px;
    background-color: #CBCBCB;
    border-radius: 2px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    margin: -6px 0;
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #FFFFFF, stop:0.5 #CFE6FD, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
    border-radius: 7px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1,
        stop:0 #F4FAFF, stop:0.5 #B7D9FB, stop:1 #7DB8F5);
    border: 1px solid #1E5FBF;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    outline-radius: 9px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:disabled {
    background: #F0F0F0;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Tables / trees
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QTableWidget, QTreeWidget {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    alternate-background-color: #E8F0FA;
    gridline-color: #D6D6D6;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #000000;
    selection-background-color: #3F88ED;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QTableWidget::item, QTreeWidget::item {
    padding: 2px 4px;
}

QTableWidget::item:hover, QTreeWidget::item:hover {
    background-color: #CFE6FD;
}

QTableWidget::item:selected, QTreeWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #3F88ED;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #FAFAFA, stop:0.5 #ECECEC, stop:1 #DDDDDD);
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    font-weight: normal;
    color: #000000;
}

QHeaderView::section:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #E1F0FE, stop:1 #B7D9FB);
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   List widget
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QListWidget {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2px;
    outline: none;
    color: #000000;
}

QListWidget::item {
    padding: 4px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #000000;
}

QListWidget::item:hover:!selected {
    background-color: #CFE6FD;
}

QListWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #3F88ED;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QListWidget::item:selected:!active {
    background-color: #3F88ED;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QListWidget:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #3F88ED;
    outline-offset: -1px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Context menus
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QMenu {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px;
    color: #000000;
}

QMenu::item {
    background: transparent;
    padding: 6px 28px 6px 14px;
    margin: 1px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #000000;
}

QMenu::item:selected {
    background-color: #CFE6FD;
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
    color: #000000;
}

QMenu::item:disabled {
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QMenu::separator {
    height: 1px;
    background-color: #D6D6D6;
    margin: 4px 8px;
}

QMenu::indicator {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    left: 4px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Progress bar -- measured pale-blue fill on white track (Backup and
   Restore dialog usage bar).
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QProgressBar {
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    text-align: center;
    color: #000000;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #9AC9F9, stop:0.5 #3F88ED, stop:1 #2A6FCB);
    border-radius: 5px;
    margin: 1px;
}

QToolTip {
    background-color: #FFFFDC;
    color: #000000;
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
}

QLabel {
    background: transparent;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #A0A0A0;
}

QSplitter::handle {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: #F0F0F0;
    width: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:1, y2:0, stop:0 #E6E6E6, stop:0.5 #F3F3F3, stop:1 #CBCBCB);
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 4px;
    min-height: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:1, y2:0, stop:0 #CFE6FD, stop:0.5 #E1F0FE, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: #F0F0F0;
    height: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #D6D6D6;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #E6E6E6, stop:0.5 #F3F3F3, stop:1 #CBCBCB);
    border: 1px solid #ACACAC;
    border-radius: 4px;
    min-width: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:0, y2:1, stop:0 #CFE6FD, stop:0.5 #E1F0FE, stop:1 #9AC9F9);
    border: 1px solid #3F88ED;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background: none;
}

QSizeGrip {
    background-color: #F0F0F0;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
}
